<title>USA: Seton Hall University, N.J., ylds 5.65 pct in 2019.</title>
<headline>Seton Hall University, N.J., ylds 5.65 pct in 2019.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Smith Barney Inc said Tuesday it tentatively priced $20.8 million New Jersey Educational Facilities Authority, for Seton Hall University, at a top yield of 5.65 percent in 2019.</p>
<p>The preliminary pricing follows:</p>
<p>NEW JERSEY EDUCATIONAL FACILITIES AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $20,790,000*</p>
<p>SETON HALL UNIVERSITY PROJECT</p>
<p>REVENUE REFUNDING BONDS</p>
<p>1996 SERIES, PROJECT E</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		 S&amp;P: AAA</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>    DATED: 10/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 01/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 07/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
